codemap 9
tour feature-select-lines
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note In the Source view, press on a line and drag to another: every line between the two, inclusive, is selected and highlighted while the button is still held, and holding the pointer above or below the code scrolls the view and keeps extending the selection. A plain click selects one line. The reader needs it to say which lines a hand-built step pins, since 'add step' adds the selected lines. Press-drag is the gesture every editor uses for a range, so the reader who tries it gets the range; before it, the drag selected only the pressed line and the range took a click, a scroll and a shift-click read off the toolbar caption. A ctrl-, alt- or double-click is a definition gesture and starts no selection; a press on the view's scrollbar scrolls and selects nothing. The selection is what the Source view's 'add step' adds and what back and forward remember.

